## Description

Fixes #20303.

`parseSelector` strips quoted strings before checking whether a selector contains a `//` or `/*` comment, so that something like `a[href^="//"]` isn't treated as a comment. The pattern `"[^"]+"|'[^']+'` needs at least one character inside the quotes, so an empty `""` or `''` wasn't matched as a string. Its closing quote then paired with the opening quote of the next string, and everything in between was removed, including the `//` comment. Since no comment was detected, the selector got parsed and the next selector ended up inside the comment:

```scss
// Input
a[href=""], // comment
foo a[href=""] {
  color: red;
}

// Output
a[href=""],
// comment foo a[href=""] {
  color: red;
}
```

The fix lets the pattern match empty strings (`[^"]*` / `[^']*`), so the selector is printed as-is, the same way `a[href], // comment` already is. The single-quote form `a[href='']` was broken too, and Less goes through the same code path, so it's fixed as well.

This came in with #17938.

